class:: PitchYIN
summary:: YIN fundamental frequency with explicit confidence and voicing
categories:: UGens>Analysis>Pitch
related:: Guides/MIR2, Classes/Pitch, Classes/Pitch2

description::
Implements the YIN difference function, cumulative mean normalized difference (CMNDF), absolute-threshold search, and parabolic period refinement described by de Cheveigné and Kawahara (2002). FFT autocorrelation and prefix energies evaluate the difference function with bounded code::N log N:: work. Confidence is code::1 - CMNDF:: at the selected period; it is not a calibrated probability.

The analyzer consumes a trailing causal frame and updates every code::hop * frameSize:: samples. First output arrives after one frame, so latency is approximately code::frameSize / sampleRate:: with no lookahead. The largest searched lag is half a frame, making the effective minimum frequency no lower than code::2 * sampleRate / frameSize::. Silence and failed voicing return three zeros.

It is practically similar to link::Classes/Pitch::, but uses YIN, never holds a stale frequency by default, and exposes continuous confidence separately from a binary voiced result.

classmethods::

method:: kr

argument:: in
Audio-rate signal. Multichannel expansion creates independent analyzers.

argument:: minFreq
Requested minimum F0 in Hz, subject to the frame-length limit described above.

argument:: maxFreq
Maximum F0 in Hz, below Nyquist.

argument:: frameSize
Literal power-of-two frame size from 256 through 8192.

argument:: hop
Update hop as a frame fraction from 0.0625 through 1.

argument:: threshold
YIN CMNDF threshold from 0.01 through 0.8. Lower values demand a deeper minimum.

returns::
An Array: frequency in Hz, CMNDF-derived confidence from 0 through 1, and voiced flag 0 or 1.

method:: latency
Returns approximate first-result latency in seconds for a sample rate and frame size.

instancemethods::

examples::
The estimated fundamental drives a sine voice, gated by the voiced decision. Listen for octave changes and tracking delay.
code::
(
Routine({
    ~mir2Buffer = Buffer.read(s, ExampleFiles.child);
    s.sync;
    ~mir2Example = {
        var source = PlayBuf.ar(1, ~mir2Buffer, BufRateScale.kr(~mir2Buffer), loop: 1);
        // For live input instead: source = SoundIn.ar(0);
        var result = PitchYIN.kr(source, 60, 1500, 2048, 0.25, 0.1);
        var tone = SinOsc.ar(result[0].clip(40, 1500).lag(0.03), 0, 0.07) * result[2].lag(0.02);
        (source * 0.12 + tone) * Line.kr(0, 1, 0.3) ! 2
    }.play;
}).play(AppClock);
)
::
code::
(
~mir2Example.free;
~mir2Buffer.free;
)
::

